s":"continuous action"}],"gloss":"rising up"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஞாயிறு","parts":[{"text":"ஞாயிறு","lemma":"ஞாயிறு","gloss":"sun"}],"gloss":"sun"},{"surface":"அனையை","parts":[{"text":"அனையை","lemma":"அனையை","gloss":"you are like"}],"gloss":"you are like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"பகைவர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"பகைவர்","lemma":"பகைவர்","gloss":"enemies"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திங்கள்","parts":[{"text":"திங்கள்","lemma":"திங்கள்","gloss":"moon"}],"gloss":"moon"},{"surface":"அனையை","parts":[{"text":"அனையை","lemma":"அனையை","gloss":"you are like"}],"gloss":"you are like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எம்மனோர்க்கே","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"our"},{"text":"அனோர்","lemma":"அனோர்","gloss":"people like"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"to"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"to people like us indeed"}]}],"literal":"Of the chest where pearl garlands hang and beauty shines, / O Valuthi of excellent quality, with long hands reaching down to the knees! / You are certainly capable of loving and protecting. / You do not know how to lie, O great lord, ever! / Like the sun that rises up, riding the ocean, with unceasing burning anger, / you are to your enemies. / Like the moon, you are to people like us!","translation":"O Valuthi of glorious excellence, whose long arms reach down to your knees, and whose chest shines with beautiful, low-hanging pearl garlands! You are indeed swift to show grace and protect those who seek you. You never know how to utter a falsehood, O great lord! To your enemies, you are like the sun that rises from the ocean, blazing with unceasing, fierce anger. But to people like us, you are like the cool, gentle moon.","modern":"முத்து மாலைகள் தொங்கும் அழகு விளங்கும் மார்பையும், முழங்கால் வரை நீளும் நீண்ட கைகளையும் உடைய, சிறந்த பண்புகள் பொருந்திய வழுதியே! நீ விரும்பி அருள் செய்வதில் வல்லவன் என்பது உண்மை. பெருமானே! நீ ஒருபோதும் பொய் சொல்ல அறியாதவன். கடல் மேல் எழுந்து வரும் தணியாத சினத்தைக் கொண்ட கதிரவனைப் போன்றவன் நீ உன்னுடைய பகைவர்களுக்கு; ஆனால் எங்களைப் போன்றவர்களுக்கு நீ குளிர்ச்சியான திங்களைப் போன்றவன்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Madurai Kūlavāṇikaṉ Cīttalaic Cāttaṉār praises the Pandya king Cittiramāṭattut Tuñciya Naṉmāṟaṉ. The poet describes the king's physical majesty, highlighting his long arms that reach his knees and his chest adorned with beautiful pearl garlands. He praises the king's absolute truthfulness and his swiftness in protecting those who seek his grace. The poem employs a striking dual metaphor to describe the king's temperament: he is like the fierce, burning sun to his enemies, but like the cool, soothing moon to his subjects and poets. This contrast beautifully illustrates the ideal qualities of a righteous ruler in the Pāṭāṇ genre, balancing fierce warrior strength with gentle benevolence.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.6],[0.6,1.4],[1.4,1.7],[1.7,2.5],[2.5,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,4.9],[4.9,5.1],[5.1,5.73],[5.73,6.0],[6.0,6.9],[6.9,7.0],[7.0,7.5],[7.5,7.9],[7.9,9.1],[9.1,9.2],[9.2,10.1],[10.1,10.4],[10.4,11.8],[11.8,12.0],[12.0,12.3],[12.3,12.64],[12.64,13.5],[13.5,13.9],[13.9,14.1],[14.1,14.3]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.7],[0.7,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,2.8],[2.8,3.37],[3.37,3.7],[3.7,4.0],[4.0,4.42],[4.42,4.83],[4.83,4.83],[4.83,6.08],[6.08,6.5],[6.5,7.44],[7.62,7.81],[8.0,8.5],[8.5,9.7],[9.7,9.8],[9.8,10.7],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,12.5],[12.5,12.8],[12.8,13.0],[13.0,13.49],[13.49,14.6],[14.6,15.0],[15.0,15.2],[15.2,15.4]]}}